emwm-utils on openSUSE
======================

xmsm is installed without the setuid bit.

Shutdown, reboot and suspend are done with "systemctl poweroff|reboot|
suspend", which logind/polkit allows for the user of the active local
session.

Screen locking is handed over to an external locker through the
lockCommand resource (added by this package). The default, set in
/usr/share/X11/app-defaults/XmSm, is:

    XmSm*lockCommand: /usr/bin/xlock -mode blank

xmsm runs it for the Lock command of xmtoolbox, after lockTimeout
seconds of inactivity, and on SIGUSR1. Any xlock mode works, e.g.
"-mode random". The executable must be given with its full path.

Using xscreensaver instead
--------------------------
Install xscreensaver, start its daemon from ~/.sessionetc:

    xscreensaver --no-splash &

and put this in ~/.Xresources:

    XmSm*lockCommand: /usr/bin/xscreensaver-command -lock
    XmSm*lockTimeout: 0
    XmSm*blankTimeout: 0

(xscreensaver then does its own blanking and timed locking.)

Built-in locker
---------------
Setting lockCommand to an empty string brings back upstream's built-in
locker. It reads /etc/shadow, so it only works if xmsm is setuid root:

    chmod u+s /usr/bin/xmsm

The package marks the file with %verify(not mode), so "rpm -V" won't
report the change, but every package update resets the mode.
